## 2026-09-03 -- Fix incomplete lookupPosting fix from PR #88 (code review)

/code-review on PR #88 (8 finder angles + verification) caught that the
previous entry's fix was incomplete. That entry fixed 'esc' from posting
detail (via postingDetailReturnScreen) and the entry into posting detail
itself (skipping loadApplication) for the new application-detail 'p'
fast path -- but three OTHER handlers still unconditionally rebuilt
a.postingDetail via lookupPosting(a.postingDetail.posting.ID) whenever
a.screen == screenPostingDetail: applicationStatusUpdatedMsg,
applicationNotesUpdatedMsg (no screen check at all), and
documentReviewCreatedMsg's screenPostingDetail branch. lookupPosting
searches a.postings, which the fast path deliberately never populates
(same reason as before) -- so lookupPosting returned a zero-value
store.Posting{}, and each of these three silently blanked the displayed
posting's title/department/location/URL after a successful status
change, notes edit, or (posting detail's own two-step) document review,
even though the underlying write succeeded. Multiple review agents
independently confirmed this, one by writing and running an actual
reproduction. My own comment on the entry-point handler had already
flagged the identical hazard for loadApplication's rebuild path and
deliberately avoided it there -- the fix just wasn't extended to these
three siblings.

Fixed with a shared rebuildPostingDetailApplication helper: instead of
re-deriving the Posting via lookupPosting (which can fail), it keeps
a.postingDetail.posting as-is (always correct, since these handlers only
ever change application-side data, never which posting is shown) and
only refreshes app/hasApp from a.applicationsByPosting -- which lookupPosting
already resolves independently of a.postings, so that half was never
broken. All three call sites now go through this one helper. Also
removed the now-dead `case screenActiveApplications:` branch in
documentReviewCreatedMsg's switch (nothing sets documentReviewReturnScreen
to that value anymore after PR #88 replaced active-applications' old 'R'
key with the application-detail flow -- confirmed via grep, only two
assignment sites remain) and tightened its `default: // screenPostingDetail`
to an explicit `case screenPostingDetail:`, since a bare default there was
silently masking exactly this class of "forgot to handle a new screen"
bug.

The review surfaced several other findings (duplicated read-and-build
logic between document_review_select.go and application_detail.go's
enterReview; a duplicated enterDocumentReviewFormMsg handler block in
app.go; application_detail.go's View() re-deriving the same Documents-
section assembly postingDetailContent already has; a missing automated
test that active-applications' glyph refreshes after a review submitted
from application detail; two test pairs that should be table-driven per
AGENTS.md; a redundant double-query when refreshing one review's glyph;
and the broader observation that the app now has three near-identical
"which screen do I return to" fields, added one at a time, which is the
root cause of the bug this entry fixes). None of these are data-
corruption bugs like the one above, and several involve real design
choices (a navigation stack instead of three fields; whether to
factor out the duplicated read-and-build logic given the two callers'
existence checks aren't quite the same shape) -- filed as GitHub issues
for follow-up rather than fixed here, to keep this fix minimal and
focused while the codebase is fresh in mind, and because the
higher-effort ones (the navigation-stack refactor especially) deserve
their own design discussion rather than an autonomous judgment call.

Verified: full build/test/lint/fmt clean. New test:
TestApp_StatusChangeFromApplicationDetailFastPath_PreservesPostingFields
(changes status from posting detail reached via application detail's
'p', asserts the posting's title survives the round trip). Manually
verified via tmux against a seeded scratch db: application detail -> 'p'
-> posting detail (fields intact) -> 's' -> pick a new status -> confirm
-- posting detail re-renders with Department/Location/title still shown
and the new status ("interviewing") applied correctly.

