documents existed on disk, regardless of review outcome, so a flagged
cover letter dropped out of the agent's queue exactly like a passed one,
with the skill having no way to know it needed another pass. Confirmed
both fixes with the user (AskUserQuestion) before implementing, since
the filter change is a real behavior change to the pinned JSON contract
(decisions.log #59), not just an additive field.

Added Candidate/Prepared.ApplicationNotes (string) and .LatestReviews
(map[store.DocumentType]LatestReview, keyed by document type). LatestReview
is a purpose-built, leaner projection of store.DocumentReview -- Outcome,
Notes, Cycle, CreatedAt -- deliberately omitting ContentSnapshot/
ContentSHA256: the agent works from the document's current content on
disk (Prepared.CoverLetter/Resume.Path), not a historical snapshot, so
shipping the full snapshot in every stage list response would just be
dead weight. Resolved via the existing store.LatestDocumentReviews (added
in #85/#86) and store.GetApplication -- N+1 per candidate with an
application, consistent with that method's own established
personal-scale-is-fine reasoning; no SQL/migration changes needed.

List()'s filter changed from "skip once both documents exist" to "skip
once both documents exist AND neither has a flagged latest review" (see
the new needsRework helper) -- a flagged document now keeps its posting
in the queue indefinitely until re-reviewed and passed, matching what
"the skill can review the status" actually requires.

Along the way, hit a real encoding/json gotcha while testing
map[store.DocumentType]LatestReview's actual output: MarshalJSON (added
in #86 for DocumentType/ReviewOutcome) is NOT consulted for map keys --
only encoding.TextMarshaler is. Without MarshalText, the map would have
silently serialized as {"0": ..., "1": ...} instead of {"cover_letter":
..., "resume": ...}, exactly the kind of silent breakage #59's own
json-tag-pinning tests exist to catch, just one layer down (map keys,
not field names). Added DocumentType.MarshalText/UnmarshalText,
verified with a test that actually marshals a map (not just a bare
value, which MarshalJSON alone already covered and would have passed
regardless).

Updated .agents/skills/apply-to-posting/SKILL.md (the documented JSON
contract) with the new fields, an explanation of what a flagged
LatestReviews entry means, and explicit revision-pass guidance ("read
the existing file's current content ... write a revised version that
addresses it -- don't start from a blank page") -- the whole point of
exposing this data is so the skill actually changes behavior when it
sees a flagged review, not just so the JSON has more fields in it.

Verified: full build/test/lint/fmt clean. New tests:
store.TestDocumentType_MarshalJSON_AsMapKey_UsesDBStringNotIntValue,
stage.TestList_IncludesApplicationNotes,
stage.TestList_IncludesLatestDocumentReviews,
stage.TestList_KeepsPostingWithBothDocumentsWhenLatestReviewIsFlagged,
stage.TestList_ExcludesPostingWithBothDocumentsWhenLatestReviewsAllPass,
stage.TestPrepare_IncludesApplicationNotesAndLatestReviews. The existing
TestCandidate_JSONShape_MatchesDocumentedAgentContract/
TestPrepared_JSONShape_MatchesDocumentedAgentContract (the #59 pinning
tests) were updated to include the two new top-level keys -- a
deliberate, expected pin change, not a loosening of the contract.
Manually verified via the built CLI against a seeded scratch db (not
just tests): `stage list` and `stage prepare` both printed
ApplicationNotes and LatestReviews.cover_letter with the exact shape
SKILL.md now documents, map key included as "cover_letter" (string, not
"0").
